WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.420
- [Instructor] Let's say we're told

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:06.420
that zero is equal to x
squared plus six x plus three,

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.040
what is an x or what our x is

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.920
that would satisfy this equation?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.800
Pause this video and try to figure it out.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.210
All right, now let's
work through it together.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.710
So the first thing that I would try to do

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.950
is see if I could factor
this right hand expression,

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.330
I have some expression,
it's equal to zero.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.620
So if I could factor it,
that might help solve.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.370
So let's see, can I think of two numbers

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.020
that when I add them, I get six,

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.000
and when I take their
product, I get positive three?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.330
Well, if I'm thinking
just in terms of integers,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.330
three is a prime number,

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.790
it only has two factors one and three.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.820
And let's see one plus
three is not equal to six,

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.480
so it doesn't look like factoring
is going to help me much.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.280
So the next thing I'll turn
to is completing the square.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.780
In fact, completing the square

00:00:53.816 --> 00:00:55.850
if there are x values that
would satisfy this equation,

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.630
completing the square
will help us solve it.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.750
And the way I do it, I'll
say zero is equal to,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.000
let me rewrite the first
part, x squared plus six x,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.630
and then I'm gonna write
the plus three out here.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.500
And my goal is to add something

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.690
to the right-hand
expression, right over here,

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.220
and then I'm gonna
subtract that same thing,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.810
so I'm not really changing the
value of the right-hand side.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.990
And I wanna add something here

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:21.150
that I'm later going to subtract,

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.370
so that what I have in
parentheses is a perfect square.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.020
Well, the way to make it a perfect square,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.860
and we've talked about
this in other videos

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.530
when we introduced ourselves
to completing the square,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.600
is we'll look at this first degree

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.330
coefficient right over
here, this positive six,

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.760
and say, okay, half of
that is positive three,

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.750
and if we were to square
that, we would get nine.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.180
So let's add a nine there.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.120
And then we could also subtract a nine.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.500
Notice, we haven't changed the value

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.850
of the right-hand side expression,

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.170
we're adding nine and
we're subtracting nine.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.460
And actually, the parentheses
are just there to help it

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.170
make a little bit more
visually clear to us,

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.760
but you don't even need the parentheses,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.610
you would essentially get the same result.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.470
But then what happens if we
simplify this a little bit?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.540
Well, what I just showed you,

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.100
let me do it in this green blue color,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.750
this thing can be rewritten
as x plus three squared.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.480
That's why we added nine there,

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.790
we said, all right, we're
gonna be dealing with a three

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.000
'cause three is half of six.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.070
And if we squared three,
we get a nine there.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.130
And then this second
part, right over here,

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.520
three minus nine, that's
equal to negative six.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.900
So we could write it like this,

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.110
zero is equal to x plus
three squared minus six.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.260
And now what we can do is
isolate this x plus three squared

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.750
by adding six to both
sides, so let's do that.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.130
Let's add six there, let's add six there.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:44.880
And what we get on the left-hand side,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.210
we get six is equal to,
on the right-hand side,

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:53.210
we just get x plus three squared.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.330
And now we can take the
square root of both sides,

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:01.300
and we could say that the plus
or minus square root of six

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.390
is equal to x plus three.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.930
And if this doesn't make full sense,

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.870
just pause the video a little
bit and think about it.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.340
If I'm saying that something
squared is equal to six,

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.070
that means that the something

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.670
is either going to be the
positive square root of six,

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.490
or the negative square root of six.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.320
And so now we can, if
we wanna solve for x,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.150
we can just subtract
three from both sides.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.653
So let's subtract three from
both sides, and what do we get?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.760
We get on the right-hand side,
we just are left with an x,

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.220
and that's going to be
equal to negative three

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.530
plus or minus the square root of six.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.750
And we are done.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.910
And obviously we could
rewrite this and say,

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.760
x could be equal to negative three

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.310
plus the square root of six,

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.610
or x could be equal to negative three

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.593
minus the square root of six.

